{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NFQSr6tKxiJ1pYpZYhxKPW","type":"tool_result","content":"/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 3  SHOOTER  (Apex Legends' movement and gunplay, without the multiplayer; first or third person). A badlands\n * two kilometres across, streamed as you go: golden grass that sways, red rock mesas in strata, dry riverbeds,\n * junipers and pines; six outposts joined by dirt roads, each with buildings to breach, containers, a watch tower with\n * a zipline and supply bins. MOVE: sprint, crouch, slide (downhill it speeds up), jump, vault low cover, mantle onto\n * ledges, climb walls, ladders, ziplines, kick doors in. FIGHT: a rifle and a shotgun (from the hip or down the\n * sights: recoil, spread, reloads), a punch with a lunge, frag grenades; raiders with shields hold five outposts, and\n * the drop point has a firing range. T switches first and third person.\n * THE 3D: the ground is a terrain (world terrain: a height and a color function, streamed in chunks for the physics\n * and the picture); the structures are one merged mesh over fixed blocks; grass is merged tufts that sway (TSL); trees\n * and rocks are shapes streamed by chunk. Every soldier is drawn by code with the pen on a procedural skeleton (feet\n * planted by IK on the ground under them, stepping round as it turns on the spot, a spine that leans and twists, hands\n * on the gun); first person draws its arms and guns with the overlay's pen, which never sinks into a wall. Muzzle\n * flashes and hits are stars of additive streaks facing the eye. A frame draws the moving things part way between the\n * last two steps (game.alpha) and turns the view by the newest mouse moves, so the motion is even at 60, 90, 144 or\n * 240 Hz; feet and hands blend into a new job instead of jumping. SHOOT.run(n): the proof's hash\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst SHOOT = (() => {\n  const M = 16;   // engine units a metre\n  /* ---- TUNING: engine units (16 a metre) and seconds ---- */\n  const GRAV = 314, JUMP = 106, WALK = 68, RUN = 118, CROUCH = 40, ADS_WALK = 46, SLIDE_BOOST = 34, SLIDE_MAX = 182, SLIDE_DRAG = 62;\n  const RADIUS = 5, HALF = 9, HALF_CROUCH = 4, HALF_SLIDE = 1.5, EYE = 26, EYE_CROUCH = 17, EYE_SLIDE = 11;\n  const MANTLE_MAX = 40, VAULT_MAX = 19, CLIMB_SPEED = 96, CLIMB_TIME = .5, LADDER_SPEED = 76, ZIP_SPEED = 200;\n  const HP = 100, SHIELD = 100, FOV = 70;\n  const N2 = E.noise2, sstep = (a, b, x) => { const t = clamp((x - a) / (b - a), 0, 1); return t * t * (3 - 2 * t); };\n  const fbm = (x, y, o) => { let v = 0, a = 1, t = 0; for (let k = 0; k < o; k++) { v += a * N2(x, y); t += a; a *= .5; x = x * 2.03 + 17.1; y = y * 2.03 + 3.7; } return v / t; };\n\n  /* =====================================================================\n   * THE BADLANDS: the ground's height and color (metres inside, engine units out), the outposts and the roads\n   * ===================================================================== */\n  const HM = 2048, SIZE = HM * M;   // the map: 2,048 metres (32,768 units) square\n  // rasters every 4 m, made once at boot: the riverbeds, the roads (how much each flattens the ground, to what height,\n  // its dirt) and the outposts' pads\n  const RS = 4, RN = HM / RS + 1, RIVER = new Float32Array(RN * RN), ROADW = new Float32Array(RN * RN), ROADH = new Float32Array(RN * RN), ROADC = new Float32Array(RN * RN), PADW = new Float32Array(RN * RN), PADH = new Float32Array(RN * RN);\n  const rs = (A, m, n) => {   // a raster at (m, n) metres, bilinear\n    const gx = clamp(m / RS, 0, RN - 1.001), gy = clamp(n / RS, 0, RN - 1.001), i = gx | 0, j = gy | 0, u = gx - i, v = gy - j, k = j * RN + i;\n    return (A[k] * (1 - u) + A[k + 1] * u) * (1 - v) + (A[k + RN] * (1 - u) + A[k + RN + 1] * u) * v;\n  };\n  const riverAt = (m, n) => 1 - sstep(.014, .05, Math.abs(fbm(m / 610 + 5.1, n / 610 + 9.7, 3) - .5));\n  /** the land before roads and pads: broad hills, mesas in two tiers with ragged cliffs, riverbeds carved flat, small\n   *  swells, and a wall of cliffs round the map's edge */\n  function baseH(m, n) {\n    let h = (fbm(m / 420, n / 420, 4) - .5) * 70;\n    const f = fbm(m / 290 + 31.7, n / 290 + 11.3, 3) + (N2(m / 21, n / 21) - .5) * .045;\n    h += sstep(.575, .6, f) * 32 + sstep(.67, .69, f) * 18;\n    h -= rs(RIVER, m, n) * 7;\n    h += (N2(m / 33, n / 33) - .5) * 3.2 + (N2(m / 9.5, n / 9.5) - .5) * .7;\n    const e = Math.min(m, n, HM - m, HM - n); h += sstep(190, 30, e) * 140 + sstep(60, 0, e) * 60;\n    return h;\n  }\n  /** the terrain's height function (engine units): the land, flattened under the roads and the outposts */\n  function height(x, y) {\n    const m = x / M, n = y / M; let h = baseH(m, n);\n    const rw = rs(ROADW, m, n); if (rw > 0) h += (rs(ROADH, m, n) - h) * rw;\n    const pw = rs(PADW, m, n); if (pw > 0) h += (rs(PADH, m, n) - h) * pw;\n    return h * M;\n  }\n  /** the terrain's color function: golden grass patched olive and dry brown, pale sand in the riverbeds, dirt roads,\n   *  gravel pads, bare earth where it steepens (the rock in strata is the terrain's own, steeper still) */\n  function color(x, y, z, nz, out) {\n13: * on the gun); first person draws its arms and guns with the overlay's pen, which never sinks into a wall. Muzzle\n404:  function noiseTex() {   // value noise that tiles (128 px), grey, filtered and mipmapped: seen from near and far\n542:      if (!s && budget > 0) { s = grass.pool.filter(p => p.used < f - 1).sort((a, b) => a.used - b.used)[0]; if (s) { if (s.key) grass.tiles.delete(s.key); buildGrass(world, s, tx, ty); grass.tiles.set(key, s); budget--; } }\n571:    const tmO = tm.clone(); tmO.colorNode = tm.colorNode; tmO.depthTest = false;   // (on the overlay a flash draws over the gun or the fist that made it)\n572:    fx.flW = flashMesh(world.scene, tm); fx.flO = flashMesh(world.overlay.scene, tmO);\n616:   *  (s 0: chips only); shards: chips thrown off it; ov: p is in the eye's frame, drawn on the overlay (over the fist that threw it) */\n716:    const h = world.ray(x, y, b.z + 14 * b.k, 0, 0, -1, 30 * b.k, { level: true });\n1009:   *  the world's flashes or the overlay's (drawFlashes) by the pen that draws the gun */\n1011:    const q = pen === world.overlay.pen ? fx.flashes.ov : fx.flashes.world; if (q.length >= FL_MAX) return;\n1067:      const h = world.ray(eye[0], eye[1], eye[2], d[0], d[1], d[2], W.far, { skip: hero });\n1143:      const h = L > 1e-4 ? world.ray(g.x, g.y, g.z, dx, dy, dz, L + 1.2, { skip: hero }) : null;\n1193:    let w = null; for (const hz of [7, 15, 24]) { w = world.ray(x, y, z + hz, f[0], f[1], 0, RADIUS + 8, o); if (w && !w.actor && Math.abs(w.nz) < .55) break; w = null; }\n1195:    const ex = w.x - w.nx * 3.5, ey = w.y - w.ny * 3.5, top = world.ray(ex, ey, z + reach + 3, 0, 0, -1, reach + 6, { skip: hero, level: true });\n1198:    if (world.ray(ex, ey, top.z + 1, 0, 0, 1, 2 * (HALF_CROUCH + RADIUS) + 1, { skip: hero, level: true })) return null;\n1199:    const bx = w.x - w.nx * 15, by = w.y - w.ny * 15, far = world.ray(bx, by, top.z + 2, 0, 0, -1, 30, { skip: hero, level: true });\n1203:  const wallAhead = (yaw) => { const h = world.ray(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 18, Math.cos(yaw), Math.sin(yaw), 0, RADIUS + 6, { skip: hero }); return h && !h.actor && Math.abs(h.nz) < .55 ? h : null; };\n1204:  const roomToStand = () => !world.ray(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 2 * (hero.half + RADIUS) - .5, 0, 0, 1, 2 * (HALF - hero.half) + 1.5, { skip: hero, level: true });\n1418:    // overlay over the fist (behind it in the world, the glove hid it); in third person on the body, chest high\n1452:    world.camera.fixed = S.cam; world.camera.near = S.cam.near;\n1461:    const hit = world.ray(piv[0], piv[1], piv[2], back[0], back[1], back[2], dist + 4, { skip: hero, level: true });\n1560:      for (const off of [0, .7, -.7, 1.4, -1.4]) { const t = ang + off * (e.strafe || 1); if (!world.ray(a.x, a.y, a.z + 8, Math.cos(t), Math.sin(t), 0, 22, { skip: a, level: true })) { ang = t; break; } }\n1576:      const h = world.ray(eye[0], eye[1], eye[2], dd[0], dd[1], dd[2], 260 * M, { skip: a }), end = h ? [h.x, h.y, h.z] : add(eye, dd, 260 * M);\n1697:   * FIRST PERSON: the arms and the gun in the overlay (its pen: x ahead of the eye, y right, z up, engine units),\n1890:    ar: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 2600, to: 380, dur: .085, vol: .5, filter: 'lowpass' }, { wave: 'square', freq: 170, to: 55, dur: .06, vol: .26 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 6400, dur: .025, vol: .16, filter: 'highpass' }],\n1891:    ar2: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 1900, to: 300, dur: .08, vol: .42, filter: 'lowpass' }, { wave: 'square', freq: 140, to: 50, dur: .05, vol: .18 }],\n1892:    sg: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 1500, to: 110, dur: .32, vol: .68, filter: 'lowpass' }, { wave: 'sine', freq: 95, to: 32, dur: .26, vol: .6 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 5000, dur: .04, vol: .2, filter: 'highpass' }],\n1903:    shieldhit: { wave: 'noise', freq: 5200, to: 3200, dur: .045, vol: .2, filter: 'highpass' },\n1904:    shieldbreak: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 6400, to: 900, dur: .36, vol: .42, filter: 'highpass' }, { wave: 'triangle', freq: 1700, to: 320, dur: .3, vol: .24 }],\n1905:    ouch: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 520, to: 200, dur: .1, vol: .36, filter: 'lowpass' }, { wave: 'sine', freq: 160, to: 90, dur: .08, vol: .3 }],\n1906:    whiz: { wave: 'noise', freq: 4600, to: 1600, dur: .09, vol: .16, filter: 'highpass' },\n1907:    hop: { wave: 'noise', freq: 900, to: 520, dur: .06, vol: .13, filter: 'lowpass' },\n1908:    mantle: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 700, to: 420, dur: .12, vol: .18, filter: 'lowpass' }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 1600, dur: .03, vol: .1, delay: .08 }],\n1909:    vault: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 1100, to: 500, dur: .1, vol: .16 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 600, dur: .06, vol: .14, delay: .12, filter: 'lowpass' }],\n1910:    slide: { wave: 'noise', freq: 900, to: 420, dur: .5, vol: .15, filter: 'lowpass' },\n1912:    kickdoor: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 720, to: 90, dur: .32, vol: .62, filter: 'lowpass' }, { wave: 'sine', freq: 120, to: 40, dur: .22, vol: .6 }, { wave: 'noise', freq: 2600, to: 600, dur: .16, vol: .26 }],\n1914:    doorshut: [{ wave: 'noise', freq: 600, to: 200, dur: .1, vol: .3, filter: 'lowpass' }, { wave: 'square', freq: 150, dur: .04, vol: .12 }],\n1942:    S.hurtT = Math.max(0, S.hurtT - dt); for (const h of S.hitDirs) h.t -= dt; S.hitDirs = S.hitDirs.filter(h => h.t > 0);\n1943:    for (const n of S.nums) n.t += dt; S.nums = S.nums.filter(n => n.t < 1.1); if (S.mark) S.mark.t -= dt;\n1944:    for (const f of S.feed) f.t -= dt; S.feed = S.feed.filter(f => f.t > 0); if (S.banner) S.banner.t -= dt;\n1987:    let cam = S.cam || w.camera.fixed;\n2012:    w.overlay.on = S.view === 'first' && S.alive;\n2013:    if (w.overlay.on) { w.overlay.camera.fov = lerp(54, 44, ease(S.adsB)); drawViewModel(w.overlay.pen, dt, cam); }\n2022:    fx.stars = fx.stars.filter(st => st.t < (st.life || 1.5 / 60));\n2034:    for (const o of OUTPOSTS) { o.spawned = false; o.left = spawns.filter(s => s.op === o.id).length; }\n2063:    world = new W3(game, { terrain: { size: SIZE, cell: 32, chunk: 32, height, color, far: 17000, physics: 1400, detail: 1.2, rock: { colors: ['#a8644a', '#c47e5a', '#8e523c', '#d0946a', '#b06e50', '#7a4632', '#c8885e'], band: 46, slope: [.34, .52] }, speckle: .2, mottle: .34 },\n2066:      torchLights: 0, glowLights: 4, lights: 3, overlay: { fov: 58 }, camera: { mode: 'fixed', capture: true, near: 1.2 }, res: 'balanced', gravity: GRAV, onDraw });\n2075:      I.move = game.input.move(); world.camera.takeMouse(I.mouse); I.stick2 = game.input.padAim;\n2079:    draw(r) { world.draw(r); r.overlay(g => hud(g, r)); },","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afaa845e-3b4d-4028-b42c-2fc9910c5b5f","uuid":"fa76dc71-4350-424e-ac42-0addeee09de9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:34:17.056Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 3  SHOOTER  (Apex Legends' movement and gunplay, without the multiplayer; first or third person). A badlands\n * two kilometres across, streamed as you go: golden grass that sways, red rock mesas in strata, dry riverbeds,\n * junipers and pines; six outposts joined by dirt roads, each with buildings to breach, containers, a watch tower with\n * a zipline and supply bins. MOVE: sprint, crouch, slide (downhill it speeds up), jump, vault low cover, mantle onto\n * ledges, climb walls, ladders, ziplines, kick doors in. FIGHT: a rifle and a shotgun (from the hip or down the\n * sights: recoil, spread, reloads), a punch with a lunge, frag grenades; raiders with shields hold five outposts, and\n * the drop point has a firing range. T switches first and third person.\n * THE 3D: the ground is a terrain (world terrain: a height and a color function, streamed in chunks for the physics\n * and the picture); the structures are one merged mesh over fixed blocks; grass is merged tufts that sway (TSL); trees\n * and rocks are shapes streamed by chunk. Every soldier is drawn by code with the pen on a procedural skeleton (feet\n * planted by IK on the ground under them, stepping round as it turns on the spot, a spine that leans and twists, hands\n * on the gun); first person draws its arms and guns with the overlay's pen, which never sinks into a wall. Muzzle\n * flashes and hits are stars of additive streaks facing the eye. A frame draws the moving things part way between the\n * last two steps (game.alpha) and turns the view by the newest mouse moves, so the motion is even at 60, 90, 144 or\n * 240 Hz; feet and hands blend into a new job instead of jumping. SHOOT.run(n): the proof's hash\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst SHOOT = (() => {\n  const M = 16;   // engine units a metre\n  