{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghk39trRieS9P2iS1kxc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 162 checks pass. Writing the dev folder's README (how to build, test and extend), then the final About text and the exit interview."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2288,"cache_read_input_tokens":946597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2288},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afaa845e-3b4d-4028-b42c-2fc9910c5b5f","uuid":"5b076910-c3c7-4644-be80-2a68a8053f02","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:38:03.719Z","request_id":"req_011Cghk39XXJkaviX4LEtej8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghk39trRieS9P2iS1kxc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wfn4DLcFLF964P9tH6XgKP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-013140__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140/README.md","content":"# SKILLER7 — Seven Killers, One Mountain (dev folder)\n\nAn original on-rails action shooter inspired by Killer7, built on my-3D2dge v0.85.2 and its 3D module. The shipped game is\nthe single file `../Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140.html` (three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3 load from\njsDelivr; everything else is inline).\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\nnode tools/fetch-deps.mjs     # once: the pinned engine handoff, 3D module, vendored three/Rapier, AI Hub client\nnode tools/patch-engine.mjs   # once: applies the // S7 PATCH: changes to engine/my-3d2dge.js\nnode tools/build.mjs          # bundle src/ + content/ and write the single HTML (fails on TODO/placeholder text or bad content)\nnode tests/run.mjs            # every test; prints only failures and one count line (--node, --browser, --only a,b)\nnode tests/run.mjs --node --only playthrough --verbose --metrics   # the bot plays the whole demo, with its progress\n```\n\n## Layout\n\n- `src/` the engine-facing code: `00-core` (bus, registries, seeded rng), `02-tuning` (dev sliders), `05-input` (preset,\n  intents, idle timer, touch-only), `10-level` (rows from rectangles, line of sight, flow fields), `11-rails`,\n  `12-camera` (generated hard-cut shots), `20-sim` … `60-save` (the deterministic sim: walker, combat, Whiteouts, bosses,\n  set pieces, gates, Room 7, story beats, saves), `70-audio`/`71-voice` (songs, SFX, laughter, Animalese voices),\n  `80-ui-kit`/`81-hud`/`82-screens`/`84-dev` (canvas UI, HUD, screens, Dev Mode, `game.debug`), `85-bot`, `86-attract`,\n  `87-hub`/`88-echorun` (AI Hub ghost mode), `90-present3d`/`92-firstperson` (the 3D presenter), `95-scenes`, `99-start`.\n- `content/` data a designer edits: `areas/*.js` (rails, gates, spots, waves, triggers, props, people), `story/*.js`\n  (talks and beats), `personas.js`, `enemies.js`, `items.js`, `shapes.js` (S7's asset set), `things3d.js`, `songs.js`,\n  `voices.js`, `about.js`.\n- `tools/validate-content.mjs` checks every area (rails, cameras' coverage, spots, waves, triggers, talks) and runs in\n  the build. Adding an area, a persona or an enemy never changes code in `src/`.\n- `tests/` `node/` (in-process with `tests/lib/node-harness.mjs`), `browser/` (headless Chromium on the built file, the\n  CDN routed to `vendor/`; `hub.test.mjs` runs the AI Hub harness on a local server), `routes/golden.js` (the bot's route).\n\n## Engine changes\n\nAll marked `// S7 PATCH:` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` (see `tools/patch-engine.mjs`): font glyphs (umlauts, accents, dashes,\n✕ ○ □ △), PlayStation as the default button symbols, Options ignored while Create is held in an AI Hub session, seven\nHumanoid hats, head and body accessories, slit eyes, a face-hiding visor, seven weapons, skis. The 3D module is unchanged.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2288,"cache_read_input_tokens":946597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2288},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afaa845e-3b4d-4028-b42c-2fc9910c5b5f","uuid":"d64e2c53-2f87-44e9-b3dd-1849de26ffa7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:38:15.354Z","request_id":"req_011Cghk39XXJkaviX4LEtej8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Wfn4DLcFLF964P9tH6XgKP":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-013140__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140/README.md","content":"# SKILLER7 — Seven Killers, One Mountain (dev folder)\n\nAn original on-rails action shooter inspired by Killer7, built on my-3D2dge v0.85.2 and its 3D module. The shipped game is\nthe single file `../Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140.html` (three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3 load from\njsDelivr; everything else is inline).\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\nnode tools/fetch-deps.mjs     # once: the pinned engine handoff, 3D module, vendored three/Rapier, AI Hub client\nnode tools/patch-engine.mjs   # once: applies the // S7 PATCH: changes to engine/my-3d2dge.js\nnode tools/build.mjs          # bundle src/ + content/ and write the single HTML (fails on TODO/placeholder text or bad content)\nnode tests/run.mjs            # every test; prints only failures and one count line (--node, --browser, --only a,b)\nnode tests/run.mjs --node --only playthrough --verbose --metrics   # the bot plays the whole demo, with its progress\n```\n\n## Layout\n\n- `src/` the engine-facing code: `00-core` (bus, registries, seeded rng), `02-tuning` (dev sliders), `05-input` (preset,\n  intents, idle timer, touch-only), `10-level` (rows from rectangles, line of sight, flow fields), `11-rails`,\n  `12-camera` (generated hard-cut shots), `20-sim` … `60-save` (the deterministic sim: walker, combat, Whiteouts, bosses,\n  set pieces, gates, Room 7, story beats, saves), `70-audio`/`71-voice` (songs, SFX, laughter, Animalese voices),\n  `80-ui-kit`/`81-hud`/`82-screens`/`84-dev` (canvas UI, HUD, screens, Dev Mode, `game.debug`), `85-bot`, `86-attract`,\n  `87-hub`/`88-echorun` (AI Hub ghost mode), `90-present3d`/`92-firstperson` (the 3D presenter), `95-scenes`, `99-start`.\n- `content/` data a designer edits: `areas/*.js` (rails, gates, spots, waves, triggers, props, people), `story/*.js`\n  (talks and beats), `personas.js`, `enemies.js`, `items.js`, `shapes.js` (S7's asset set), `things3d.js`, `songs.js`,\n  `voices.js`, `about.js`.\n- `tools/validate-content.mjs` checks every area (rails, cameras' coverage, spots, waves, triggers, talks) and runs in\n  the build. Adding an area, a persona or an enemy never changes code in `src/`.\n- `tests/` `node/` (in-process with `tests/lib/node-harness.mjs`), `browser/` (headless Chromium on the built file, the\n  CDN routed to `vendor/`; `hub.test.mjs` runs the AI Hub harness on a local server), `routes/golden.js` (the bot's route).\n\n## Engine changes\n\nAll marked `// S7 PATCH:` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` (see `tools/patch-engine.mjs`): font glyphs (umlauts, accents, dashes,\n✕ ○ □ △), PlayStation as the default button symbols, Options ignored while Create is held in an AI Hub session, seven\nHumanoid hats, head and body accessories, slit eyes, a face-hiding visor, seven weapons, skis. The 3D module is unchanged.\n"}}}
