{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghk4BsBgt8uq3erPNQyP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PbH6wuYWPtr2EDDkrgSmHM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, re\np='content/about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(key_start, new_value):\n    global s\n    i = s.index(key_start); j = s.index(\"'],\", i)\n    s = s[:i] + new_value + s[j:]\nrep(\"['Testing', '\", \"['Testing', 'One command, node tests/run.mjs: 162 checks in 7 suites. Node (in a vm, driven by game.advance and game.debug): content validation; every area, node and boss phase; the systems (rails, aim, weapons, the scan, Whiteouts, crits, personas, freezing, gates, healing, saves, story skipping, dev sliders, voices, determinism); attract mode for 190 s; solo Echo Run; the AI Hub flow against a stand-in hub; and a scripted playthrough where an honest bot plays the whole demo on Piste from the cold open to the credits. Browser (headless Chromium 1243, Playwright 1.63.0, file://, the CDN routed to local copies): boot, keyboard play, the pause menu, Skip scene, Dev Mode sliders, mouse picking of rail junctions, attract from idle, PlayStation and Xbox glyphs with a stand-in DualSense, the touch-only notice; the AI Hub harness at 2 players, at 4 players with latency 150, jitter 50 and loss 5, and host-leave. Screenshot reviews of every area, set piece and screen.\")\nrep(\"['Research', '\", \"['Research', 'None beyond the provided plan, the engine\\\\'s handoff documents (README, API card and index, AI guide, asset card, the 3D module\\\\'s header and starter slices) and the AI Hub README.\")\ns = re.sub(r\"  testing: \\[.*?\\n  \\],\\n\", lambda m: \"\"\"  testing: [\n    ['How many issues did testing catch?', 'About forty during the build: the content validator caught a missing area; the bot\\\\'s playthrough about fourteen (softlocks, boss balance, unreachable things); the system suites four; the browser suites and screenshot reviews about twenty (layout, cameras inside walls, input timing, state leaking between scenes, the hub\\\\'s progress reports).'],\n    ['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?', 'Nine: every shot flew 3 degrees high (the recoil kicked before the ray left); no results after Grau (target 0 read as false), which stranded the player; the Palais safe out of reach; two things at one stop with only the nearest selectable; Room 7 doors shut by Whiteouts 200 m away; the Avalaugh\\\\'s warm spots buried inside its body, so it could not be beaten; the cel filter drawing black without a GPU; Escape opening the pause menu under open screens; and the hub\\\\'s progress reports missing, which failed its check.'],\n    ['What was the most helpful test you ran?', 'The scripted playthrough: an honest bot playing the whole demo through the same intents a player makes. It found every softlock and the boss balance problems.'],\n    ['What was the least helpful test you ran?', 'Headless screenshots for judging the look: SwiftShader draws a few frames a second and renders post filters black, so the pictures said little about a real screen.']\n  ],\n\"\"\", s, flags=re.S)\ns = re.sub(r\"  engine: \\[.*?\\n  \\],\\n\", lambda m: \"\"\"  engine: [\n    ['What did you like most about the engine?', 'That the 2D engine and its 3D module are one engine: fixed steps, input with rebinding, the pause menu, settings, saves, the rigs and the music clock carried straight into a 3D game, and the rigs drawn as cards gave the characters a look for free.'],\n    ['Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'Yes. The 3D module\\\\'s post filters render black in headless Chromium without a GPU, so I added a probe that falls back to the clean picture; a block of one stairs character is one flight, not a step per tile; the Shell\\\\'s theme font wants a family list, not a font shorthand; and a frame is capped at 50 ms, so under a slow GPU game time crawls and tests had to wait on state, not time.'],\n    ['What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?', 'The rail system and its camera director: rails, junctions, ski physics, lifts and jumps, and Killer7-style hard-cut shots generated for every stretch of rail and checked for line of sight.'],\n    ['What was the hardest part about using the engine?', 'Building a 3D game on a 2D-first API from documentation spread over several files, and keeping a deterministic sim apart from a presenter that cannot be read back.'],\n    ['What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)', 'Every change is marked // S7 PATCH: in my-3d2dge.js. Font glyphs for umlauts, accents, dashes and the PlayStation symbols the prompts need; PlayStation as the default button symbols; in an AI Hub session Options is ignored while Create is held; seven new Humanoid hats; head and body accessories (goggles, moustache, beard, cigar, grin, shades, pack, bandolier, badge, braces, camera); slit eyes; a visor that hides the face; seven new weapons (revolver, pistol, rifle, shotgun, ski poles, alphorn, launcher); and skis. The 3D module is unchanged.'],\n    ['If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?', 'A rail-and-camera primitive for cinematic games (shots along a path with line-of-sight checks), and post filters that fall back by themselves where the GPU path fails.']\n  ],\n\"\"\", s, flags=re.S)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs && node -e \"\nconst vm=require('vm'),fs=require('fs');const ctx={console:{log(){},warn(){},error(){}}};ctx.globalThis=ctx;vm.createContext(ctx);\nvm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('engine/my-3d2dge.js','utf8'),ctx);vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('out/bundle.js','utf8'),ctx);\nconst A=ctx.S7.ABOUT; console.log(A.source.length, A.testing.length, A.engine.length, A.prompt.length); fs.writeFileSync('out/about.json', JSON.stringify(A, null, 1));\"","description":"Write the final About text and export it","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1568,"cache_read_input_tokens":948885,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1568},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afaa845e-3b4d-4028-b42c-2fc9910c5b5f","uuid":"78935ddf-635a-4593-a1ce-5eb52433d19a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:38:44.493Z","request_id":"req_011Cghk4BPQwwfpP84SvLtiz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PbH6wuYWPtr2EDDkrgSmHM":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-013140__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140 && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, re\np='content/about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(key_start, new_value):\n    global s\n    i = s.index(key_start); j = s.index(\"'],\", i)\n    s = s[:i] + new_value + s[j:]\nrep(\"['Testing', '\", \"['Testing', 'One command, node tests/run.mjs: 162 checks in 7 suites. Node (in a vm, driven by game.advance and game.debug): content validation; every area, node and boss phase; the systems (rails, aim, weapons, the scan, Whiteouts, crits, personas, freezing, gates, healing, saves, story skipping, dev sliders, voices, determinism); attract mode for 190 s; solo Echo Run; the AI Hub flow against a stand-in hub; and a scripted playthrough where an honest bot plays the whole demo on Piste from the cold open to the credits. Browser (headless Chromium 1243, Playwright 1.63.0, file://, the CDN routed to local copies): boot, keyboard play, the pause menu, Skip scene, Dev Mode sliders, mouse picking of rail junctions, attract from idle, PlayStation and Xbox glyphs with a stand-in DualSense, the touch-only notice; the AI Hub harness at 2 players, at 4 players with latency 150, jitter 50 and loss 5, and host-leave. Screenshot reviews of every area, set piece and screen.\")\nrep(\"['Research', '\", \"['Research', 'None beyond the provided plan, the engine\\\\'s handoff documents (README, API card and index, AI guide, asset card, the 3D module\\\\'s header and starter slices) and the AI Hub README.\")\ns = re.sub(r\"  testing: \\[.*?\\n  \\],\\n\", lambda m: \"\"\"  testing: [\n    ['How many issues did testing catch?', 'About forty during the build: the content validator caught a missing area; the bot\\\\'s playthrough about fourteen (softlocks, boss balance, unreachable things); the system suites four; the browser suites and screenshot reviews about twenty (layout, cameras inside walls, input timing, state leaking between scenes, the hub\\\\'s progress reports).'],\n    ['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?', 'Nine: every shot flew 3 degrees high (the recoil kicked before the ray left); no results after Grau (target 0 read as false), which stranded the player; the Palais safe out of reach; two things at one stop with only the nearest selectable; Room 7 doors shut by Whiteouts 200 m away; the Avalaugh\\\\'s warm spots buried inside its body, so it could not be beaten; the cel filter drawing black without a GPU; Escape opening the pause menu under open screens; and the hub\\\\'s progress reports missing, which failed its check.'],\n    ['What was the most helpful test you ran?', 'The scripted playthrough: an honest bot playing the whole demo through the same intents a player makes. It found every softlock and the boss balance problems.'],\n    ['What was the least helpful test you ran?', 'Headless screenshots for judging the look: SwiftShader draws a few frames a second and renders post filters black, so the pictures said little about a real screen.']\n  ],\n\"\"\", s, flags=re.S)\ns = re.sub(r\"  engine: \\[.*?\\n  \\],\\n\", lambda m: \"\"\"  engine: [\n    ['What did you like most about the engine?', 'That the 2D engine and its 3D module are one engine: fixed steps, input with rebinding, the pause menu, settings, saves, the rigs and the music clock carried straight into a 3D game, and the rigs drawn as cards gave the characters a look for free.'],\n    ['Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'Yes. The 3D module\\\\'s post filters render black in headless Chromium without a GPU, so I added a probe that falls back to the clean picture; a block of one stairs character is one flight, not a step per tile; the Shell\\\\'s theme font wants a family list, not a font shorthand; and a frame is capped at 50 ms, so under a slow GPU game time crawls and tests had to wait on state, not time.'],\n    ['What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?', 'The rail system and its camera director: rails, junctions, ski physics, lifts and jumps, and Killer7-style hard-cut shots generated for every stretch of rail and checked for line of sight.'],\n    ['What was the hardest part about using the engine?', 'Building a 3D game on a 2D-first API from documentation spread over several files, and keeping a deterministic sim apart from a presenter that cannot be read back.'],\n    ['What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)', 'Every change is marked // S7 PATCH: in my-3d2dge.js. Font glyphs for umlauts, accents, dashes and the PlayStation symbols the prompts need; PlayStation as the default button symbols; in an AI Hub session Options is ignored while Create is held; seven new Humanoid hats; head and body accessories (goggles, moustache, beard, cigar, grin, shades, pack, bandolier, badge, braces, camera); slit eyes; a visor that hides the face; seven new weapons (revolver, pistol, rifle, shotgun, ski poles, alphorn, launcher); and skis. The 3D module is unchanged.'],\n    ['If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?', 'A rail-and-camera primitive for cinematic games (shots along a path with line-of-sight checks), and post filters that fall back by themselves where the GPU path fails.']\n  ],\n\"\"\", s, flags=re.S)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs && node -e \"\nconst vm=require('vm'),fs=require('fs');const ctx={console:{log(){},warn(){},error(){}}};ctx.globalThis=ctx;vm.createContext(ctx);\nvm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('engine/my-3d2dge.js','utf8'),ctx);vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync('out/bundle.js','utf8'),ctx);\nconst A=ctx.S7.ABOUT; console.log(A.source.length, A.testing.length, A.engine.length, A.prompt.length); fs.writeFileSync('out/about.json', JSON.stringify(A, null, 1));\"","description":"Write the final About text and export it","timeout":120000}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01PbH6wuYWPtr2EDDkrgSmHM":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-013140__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140"}}}
