DME, API card and index, AI guide, asset card, the 3D module\\'s header and starter slices) and the AI Hub README.'],","     ['Environment', 'Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown'],","     ['Model', 'Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh'],","     ['Usage', 'unknown']","   ],","   testing: [","-    ['How many issues did testing catch?', 'About forty during the build: the content validator caught missing areas and walls across rails, the Node suites caught softlocks and state bugs, and the browser runs caught black frames and layout overlaps.'],","-    ['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?', 'About eight: the Comic cel filter drawing a black screen on a GPU-less browser, scenes and boot order, a pause-menu edge case, softlocks in the scripted playthrough, and cameras inside walls.'],","-    ['What was the most helpful test you ran?', 'The scripted playthrough: an honest bot playing the whole demo through the same intents a player makes, which found every softlock.'],","-    ['What was the least helpful test you ran?', 'Pixel screenshots in headless Chromium for look checks: SwiftShader draws without a GPU, so post filters came out black and the pictures said little about a real screen.']","+    ['How many issues did testing catch?', 'About forty during the build: the content validator caught a missing area; the bot\\'s playthrough about fourteen (softlocks, boss balance, unreachable things); the system suites four; the browser suites and screenshot reviews about twenty (layout, cameras inside walls, input timing, state leaking between scenes, the hub\\'s progress reports).'],","+    ['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?', 'Nine: every shot flew 3 degrees high (the recoil kicked before the ray left); no results after Grau (target 0 read as false), which stranded the player; the Palais safe out of reach; two things at one stop with only the nearest selectable; Room 7 doors shut by Whiteouts 200 m away; the Avalaugh\\'s warm spots buried inside its body, so it could not be beaten; the cel filter drawing black without a GPU; Escape opening the pause menu under open screens; and the hub\\'s progress reports missing, which failed its check.'],","+    ['What was the most helpful test you ran?', 'The scripted playthrough: an honest bot playing the whole demo through the same intents a player makes. It found every softlock and the boss balance problems.'],","+    ['What was the least helpful test you ran?', 'Headless screenshots for judging the look: SwiftShader draws a few frames a second and renders post filters black, so the pictures said little about a real screen.']","   ],","   engine: [","-    ['What did you like most about the engine?', 'That the 2D engine and its 3D module are one engine: fixed steps, input with rebinding, the pause menu, settings, saves, rigs and the music clock all carried straight into a 3D game, and the rigs drawn as cards gave the characters a look for free.'],","-    ['Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'Yes: the 3D module\\'s post-processing filters render black in headless Chromium without a GPU, so I added a probe that falls back to the clean filter; and the level text format treats a block of one stairs character as a single flight, which I first guessed was per tile.'],","-    ['What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?', 'The rail system with its camera director: rails, junctions, ski physics and lifts, and Killer7-style hard-cut shots generated per stretch of rail and checked for line of sight.'],","-    ['What was the hardest part about using the engine?', 'Working out a 3D game on a 2D-first API surface from documentation spread over several files, and keeping a deterministic sim separate from a presenter that cannot be read back.'],","-    ['What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)', 'Every change is marked // S7 PATCH: in my-3d2dge.js. Font glyphs for umlauts, accents, dashes and the PlayStation symbols the prompts need; PlayStation as the default button symbols; in an AI Hub session Options is ignored while Create is held; seven new Humanoid hats; head and body accessories (goggles, moustache, beard, cigar, grin, shades, pack, bandolier, badge, braces, camera); slit eyes; a visor that hides the face; seven new weapons (revolver, pistol, rifle, shotgun, ski poles, alphorn, launcher); skis.'],","-    ['If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?', 'A rail-and-camera primitive for cinematic games (shots along a path with line-of-sight checks), and post filters that degrade gracefully where the GPU path fails.']","+    ['What did you like most about the engine?', 'That the 2D engine and its 3D module are one engine: fixed steps, input with rebinding, the pause menu, settings, saves, the rigs and the music clock carried straight into a 3D game, and the rigs drawn as cards gave the characters a look for free.'],","+    ['Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'Yes. The 3D module\\'s post filters render black in headless Chromium without a GPU, so I added a probe that falls back to the clean picture; a block of one stairs character is one flight, not a step per tile; the Shell\\'s theme font wants a family list, not a font shorthand; and a frame is capped at 50 ms, so under a slow GPU game time crawls and tests had to wait on state, not time.'],","+    ['What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?', 'The rail system and its camera director: rails, junctions, ski physics, lifts and jumps, and Killer7-style hard-cut shots generated for every stretch of rail and checked for line of sight.'],","+    ['What was the hardest part about using the engine?', 'Building a 3D game on a 2D-first API from documentation spread over several files, and keeping a deterministic sim apart from a presenter that cannot be read back.'],","+    ['What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)', 'Every change is marked // S7 PATCH: in my-3d2dge.js. Font glyphs for umlauts, accents, dashes and the PlayStation symbols the prompts need; PlayStation as the default button symbols; in an AI Hub session Options is ignored while Create is held; seven new Humanoid hats; head and body accessories (goggles, moustache, beard, cigar, grin, shades, pack, bandolier, badge, braces, camera); slit eyes; a visor that hides the face; seven new weapons (revolver, pistol, rifle, shotgun, ski poles, alphorn, launcher); and skis. The 3D module is unchanged.'],","+    ['If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?', 'A rail-and-camera primitive for cinematic games (shots along a path with line-of-sight checks), and post filters that fall back by themselves where the GPU path fails.']","   ],","   prompt: [","     ['What did you like most about this prompt?', 'Its clarity about the finished product: a complete vertical slice with dev tools, attract mode, multiplayer and controller-first UX, plus a detailed plan to build from.'],"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-023153__x696bb3/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-013140__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140.html","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-013140__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140/content/about.js","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-013140__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140/out/about.json","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-013140__x696bb3/work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140/out/bundle.js"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PbH6wuYWPtr2EDDkrgSmHM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
