ifts and jumps, and Killer7-style hard-cut shots generated for every stretch of rail and checked for line of sight.'],","     ['What was the hardest part about using the engine?', 'Building a 3D game on a 2D-first API from documentation spread over several files, and keeping a deterministic sim apart from a presenter that cannot be read back.'],","-    ['What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)', 'Every change is marked // S7 PATCH: in my-3d2dge.js. Font glyphs for umlauts, accents, dashes and the PlayStation symbols the prompts need; PlayStation as the default button symbols; in an AI Hub session Options is ignored while Create is held; seven new Humanoid hats; head and body accessories (goggles, moustache, beard, cigar, grin, shades, pack, bandolier, badge, braces, camera); slit eyes; a visor that hides the face; seven new weapons (revolver, pistol, rifle, shotgun, ski poles, alphorn, launcher); and skis. The 3D module is unchanged.'],","+    ['What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)', 'Every change is marked // S7 PATCH: in my-3d2dge.js. Font glyphs for umlauts, accents, dashes and the PlayStation symbols the prompts need; PlayStation as the default button symbols; in an AI Hub session Options is ignored while Create is held; seven new Humanoid hats; head and body accessories (goggles, moustache, beard, cigar, grin, shades, pack, bandolier, badge, braces, camera); slit eyes; a visor that hides the face; seven new weapons (revolver, pistol, rifle, shotgun, ski poles, alphorn, launcher); skis; and one doc comment reworded. The 3D module is unchanged.'],","     ['If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?', 'A rail-and-camera primitive for cinematic games (shots along a path with line-of-sight checks), and post filters that fall back by themselves where the GPU path fails.']","   ],","   prompt: ["]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-013140__x696bb3/wo