{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - User invoked `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\" A session Stop hook blocks stopping until met (auto-clears; don't tell the user to run /goal clear).\n   - STAGE.md: \"Read TASK.md (what to build) and PLAN.md (how to build it, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort) in this folder. Build the game TASK.md describes, following the plan and using the title it gives; where they disagree, TASK.md wins. Deliver everything TASK.md asks for, including its file name, and the sections it asks for in your final reply.\"\n   - TASK.md: source Killer7; title riff (plan picked \"Skiller7\" via RNG); single HTML `Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140.html` in root; dev subfolder `Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140/`; built on my-3d2dge handoff (engine changes allowed); native art/animation plus new; all audio in code, Animalese/Simlish voices; AI Hub multiplayer (lib/hub) and game on its own; dev mode from pause with live sliders + reset; attract mode after 10 s idle (any input exits); 10-foot controller-first UI (PS glyphs, Xbox option, keyboard/mouse native, hover focuses); touch-only shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" + settings button, attract still runs; no TODOs/placeholders/stubs; Source Information/Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback in chat reply and in-game About/Credits; exit-interview.json in exact shape.\n   - Security/process constraints from TASK.md (preserve): \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\" Also: \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\" Tests: \"Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers.\"\n   - Source Information fields required: Date 2026-11-04 01:31:40; Source; Plan; Genre and Perspective; Tech; Art Direction; Animation; Audio; Online; Testing; Research; Environment \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\"; Model \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\"; Usage (only if estimates available, else unknown).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 2D engine (E.Game fixed 1/120 s steps, scenes, input presets/rebinding, E.Shell pause/settings/controls/saves, game.saves, game.debug, Humanoid rigs, E.Blob, audio music clock/layers/tempo, E.font) + its 3D module (E.World3D: level rows/legend or terrain height fn, actors as cards with pose:false, world.pen per-frame drawing, world.glow, world.light, world.overlay first-person pen, camera 'fixed', world.project, Comic cel post filter).\n   - three.js r182 + Rapier 0.19.3 via jsDelivr import map; tests route CDN to vendor/.\n   - Deterministic sim (no Math.random; S7.RNG named mulberry32 streams) separated from Presenter3D/NullPresenter; event bus S7.bus.\n   - Rails (RailGraph/RailPath catmull dense sampling), walker, junctions, ski physics, lifts, jumps; CameraDirector generating hard-cut shots per edge with LOS validation; area camera hooks.\n   - Whiteouts invisible until revealed (scan/flare/echo/flash), warm spots = instant crit; personas with weapons/skills; Featherbed ring; freezing + Sweep rescue; gates; Room 7; story talks/beats as generators; saves.\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 ghost mode (Echo Run): connect/ready/start/time/send/progress/result/time-up/end/leave; harness.html checks.\n   - Bot (honest/cheating) for playthrough test and attract mode.\n   - Engine patches marked `// S7 PATCH:`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (dev folder = `work/Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140/`):\n   - Deliverables in work root: `Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140.html` (~2.1 MB, built), `exit-interview.json` (generated, parses).\n   - `tools/fetch-deps.mjs` (pinned commits engine 4390a98…, ai-hub f8835e4…), `tools/patch-engine.mjs` (idempotent patches: S7_GLYPHS font incl. ÄÖÜÈÉÀäöüèéàßçô—–…·’‘“”✕○□△◆■●°; glyphs default 'playstation'; S7_hubCreate pause rule; weapon list + S7_WEAPONS; _s7Head/_s7Body/_s7Weapon/_s7Skis methods; hats beanie/ushanka/felt/beret/hardhat/racehelmet/pillbox; slit eyes; visor hides face; reworded engine version doc comment \"a stand-in in the repo … (S7 PATCH: comment reworded)\"), `tools/build.mjs` (concatenates src/0-8, content/** sorted, src/9 into IIFE; inlines hub session.js first in head, hub meta tags, importmap, engine, asset sets kenney-holiday/kenney-furniture/kaykit-furniture-bits/kenney-nature, bundle, 3D module as inline module, `S7.start({ World3D: My3D2dge.World3D })`, 20 s watchdog; fails on TODO/FIXME/TBD/XXX/lorem/placeholder in our files; runs validator; `--dev` allowed scaffold, scaffold since deleted), `tools/validate-content.mjs`, `tools/exit-interview.mjs` (builds exit-interview.json from out/about.json; checks non-empty fields except aiHub.series).\n   - `src/`: 00-core.js, 02-tuning.js (TUNING sliders, CHEATS, DIFF), 05-input.js (INPUT preset incl. p1..p7, d0/d8/d9, wall-clock idle timer with reset(), pointerdown any-input, readIntents, noIntents), 10-level.js (buildRows; stairs one spec per block with box; LevelGrid floorAt/solidAt/ray/los (terrain adaptive step L/60)/flow/flowDir), 11-rails.js (RailPath, RailGraph; lift `ground` flag), 12-camera.js (CameraDirector with low/wide candidates scaled outdoors, clearance & ceiling checks, pullIn/aimSafe, project/unproject), 20-sim.js (Sim class; resetTransient(); walker, junction 0.3 s beat, ski, jump speed 420, statueAtNode stop, triggers (skipped in echo), waves, anyAlive(r=40), area update hook, camera incl. areaDef.camera), 21-combat.js (aim, weapons — ray before recoil, hitscan with burn/knock, shield-first rayHits, embedded boss warm spots win, cone, lob, explode, projectiles, hits/crits/kills, drops, hurt, reveals incl. flash timer, skills, economy), 30-whiteouts.js (spawn, warmPos, AI: walker/runner/sled/thrower/twins/plow/inspector/bloom/dancer/crawler/idle, burst), 33-bosses.js (Grau 3 phases tuned: throws 1.05/.85 s, dmg 8, hat window 1.5/1.2 s, body open only in hat window, phase 3 car at FLOORS[0], drops every 8 s; Band: windows from track sounding, dancers every 2 bars max 4; Hansi: Avalaugh 5 spots/thaw/buds capped 4, slalom with gates & retry, interview framing at 2.3 m; finishTarget), 35-setpieces.js (LAWINE update/camera, gondola update (cabinPos uses sim.hero)/camera, summit camera via aimSafe, THINGS3D drift/gateslots/echowall/icelock/chessboard/pistepoles/avalanche/cablecar/slalomgates/avalaugh/chairlift, BOSS3D grau/band, drawAreaHud), 40-meta.js (nearList + facing-based focus, interact(pick), gates, pickups, ring/switch, freeze/rescue, Room 7, Murmel, useExit echo finish), 50-story.js (talks, choices, cards, beats, skipCutscene, objectives), 60-save.js, 70-audio.js, 71-voice.js, 80-ui-kit.js, 81-hud.js, 82-screens.js (modals: difficulty, wax, wardrobe, map, dossier, personas, codelock, postcard, exposure, about), 84-dev.js (DevModal; Backspace resets without closing; warp/warpBoss using resetTransient; hash; debugHandle; sceneName), 85-bot.js, 86-attract.js (S7.attractInfo), 87-hub.js (wall-clock sends/progress), 88-echorun.js, 90-present3d.js (probe after draw; boss actors, ghosts, effects, Ansel toboggan), 92-firstperson.js, 95-scenes.js (S7.ui with pausable guard, freeCam, drawRank, scenes title/play/results/gameover/credits, titleBackdrop), 99-start.js (SETTINGS, HELP, S7.start, shell theme with family-only fonts + zoom, newGame/continueGame, pointerLock, registerShapes).\n   - `content/`: personas.js, enemies.js, items.js, shapes.js (S7 set), things3d.js (cablecar duplicate removed), voices.js, songs.js, about.js (final ABOUT text, Usage \"Session time about 2 h 15 min (2026-11-04 01:31 to about 03:46). API cost and token counts: unknown.\"), areas/room7.js, 00A-lobby.js, 00B-thirdfloor.js (+00C with camera), 01A-village.js, 01B-palais.js (safe at [18.6,29.2], band camera), 01C-blackrun.js, 01D-gondola.js, 01E-archive.js (+01F), story/common.js, t00.js, t01.js.\n   - `tests/`: run.mjs (one command), lib/node-harness.mjs (globals option), lib/browser.mjs, lib/png.mjs, node/areas, content, modes, playthrough, systems; browser/ui, hub; routes/golden.js. README.md in dev folder. spike/ and tmp/ deleted.\n\n4. Errors and fixes (main): cel post filter black headless → probe fallback to 'clean' (moved after w.draw so real GPUs read the current frame); stairs per-block semantics; undefined legend keys deleted; THINGS3D defined early; performance missing → loop option only if defined; camera too close/top-down → new candidates & clearance; HUD overlaps; recoil applied before ray; bot persona/shoot order, goto after exit, auto-fire fireD, lob pitch, prefer open warm spots, heal in boss; Grau overpowering → rebalance; resultsReady 0 falsy; safe out of reach; multiple interactables