 in the pause menu; Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (2D engine with all modules, patched) and its 3D module v0.85.2; three.js r182 (WebGPU renderer, WebGL 2 fallback) and Rapier 0.19.3 from jsDelivr; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; plain JavaScript in one HTML file; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 (Chromium) for tests; Art Direction: engine native style, PS1-resolution 3D picture, rigs on cards, ink outlines, Comic cel filter where the device can draw it (falls back by itself); white snow, black shadows, saturated red; new hats/accessories/weapons/skis; ~sixty new shapes; pen-drawn machinery; Animation: engine procedural rigs + patches; skiing crouch/tuck, quick turns, switch flurries, freezing/thawing, giggle-ups, melting; first-person weapons with bob/sway/kick/reloads; Audio: all code — step-notation songs with explore/danger layers (hotel lounge, oompah polka, band tracks as weak spots), chip SFX, WebAudio laughter synth (4 styles, positional, muffled behind walls), Animalese gibberish voices letter by letter, wind/room-tone beds; Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1 ghost mode Echo Run (1–4 players as echoes); solo Echo Run vs recorded best; Testing: one command node tests/run.mjs, 162 checks in 7 suites (Node: content, areas/bosses, systems, attract 190 s, Echo Run, hub stand-in, scripted honest-bot playthrough; Browser headless Chromium 1243/Playwright 1.63.0 file:// CDN routed: boot, keyboard play, pause, Skip scene, Dev Mode sliders, mouse junction picking, attract from idle, PS/Xbox glyphs with stand-in DualSense, touch-only notice; AI Hub harness 2p, 4p with latency 150/jitter 50/loss 5, host-leave; screenshot reviews); Research: none beyond plan, engine handoff docs (README, API card/index, AI guide, asset card, 3D module header and starter slices) and AI Hub README; Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown; Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh; Usage: Session time about 2 h 15 min (01:31 to ~03:46); API cost and token counts unknown.\n     - Testing Feedback: (1) About forty (validator 1 missing area; playthrough ~14; system suites 4; browser/screenshots ~20). (2) Nine critical: shots 3° high (recoil before ray); no results after Grau (target 0 falsy) stranding player; Palais safe out of reach; only nearest of two interactables selectable; Room 7 doors shut by Whiteouts 200 m away; Avalaugh warm spots inside its body (unbeatable); cel filter black without GPU; Escape opening pause under open screens; hub progress reports missing (failed hub check). (3) Most helpful: scripted honest-bot playthrough. (4) Least helpful: headless screenshots for judging the look (SwiftShader slow, post filters black).\n     - Engine Feedback: (1) 2D engine + 3D module as one engine (fixed steps, input/rebinding, pause, settings, saves, rigs, music clock; rigs as cards). (2) Yes: post filters black headless → probe fallback; stairs block = one flight; Shell theme font wants family list; 50 ms frame cap makes game time crawl under slow GPU so tests wait on state. (3) Rail system + camera director. (4) 3D game on 2D-first API from docs across files; deterministic sim apart from presenter. (5) All `// S7 PATCH:` changes listed (font glyphs, PS default glyphs, Options ignored while Create held in hub session, 7 hats, accessories, slit eyes, visor, 7 weapons, skis; 3D module unchanged). (6) Rail-and-camera primitive; post filters that fall back by themselves.\n     - Prompt Feedback: (1) Clarity about finished product + detailed plan. (2) Plan written for another run's names/model/date; \"Online\" multiplayer library vs single-player source. (3) Building the whole plan at once: ten areas, three bosses, seven characters, all systems. (4) Scope plan to time / name priority features; say whether headless screenshots judge look.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Write the final reply (text only) with the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections using exactly the text above, plus a short note on deliverables (`Skiller7-Killer7-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-013140.html` and `exit-interview.json` in the work root; dev folder with `node tools/build.mjs` and `node tests/run.mjs`; final result \"162 passed, 0 failed\"). This directly completes the goal condition: \"your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build--20261104-013140--x696bb3-work/afaa845e-3b4d-4028-b42c-2fc9910c5b5f.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afaa845e-3b4d-4028-b42c-2fc9910c5b5f","uuid":"71ad11f4-e171-49da-bd46-42f9477ec99d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:46:41.142Z","isSynthetic":true}
