{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019mGXzpodmxPVYDenXe5Pnp","type":"tool_result","content":"      if (game.input.touchEnabled !== undefined) game.input.touchEnabled = false;\n    },\n    update(dt) {\n      S7.Input.tick(dt); titleT += dt;\n      sim.update(dt, S7.noIntents()); pres.step(dt); snd();\n      const m = S7.ui.modal;\n      if (m) {\n        S7.ui.update();\n        if (!S7.ui.modal && S7.ui.kind === null && m instanceof DifficultyModal && m.result && m.result !== 'back') { S7.newGame(m.result); return; }\n        \n      } else {\n        const touch = S7.touchOnly();\n        if (touch) { const c = game.input.clicked && game.input.clicked(); if (c && UI.hit(c, ...(this.setBox || [0, 0, 0, 0]))) game.menu('settings'); }\n        else titleMenu.update(UI.nav(game), game);\n      }\n      if (game.shell && game.shell.screen) S7.Input.idleShell = (S7.Input.idleShell || 0) + dt; else S7.Input.idleShell = 0;\n      if (S7.Input.idle > 10 && !S7.inSession) { if (S7.ui.modal) S7.ui.close(); if (game.shell && game.shell.screen) game.shell.hide(); game.go('attract', {}); }\n    },\n    draw(r) {\n      pres.draw(r);\n      r.overlay(g => {\n        UI.veil(g, r, .35, '#05030a');\n        const S = UI.safe(r);\n        UI.title(g, 'SKILLER', r.W / 2 - 14, S.y0 + 8, 5);\n        E.font.title(g, '7', r.W / 2 + E.font.width('SKILLER', { scale: 5 }) / 2 - 6, S.y0 + 8, { scale: 5, colors: ['#ff5060', '#d81e2a', '#a01018'], outline: INK, depth: 2, depthColor: '#2a0a0e' });\n2: * intents; the bot makes the same intents), last-device tracking for prompts, the idle timer for attract mode, and the\n40:  sawKey: false, sawPad: false, idle: 0, lastReal: 0, wheel: 0, flickT: 0, flickArmed: true, aimToggled: false,\n41:  /** hooked once at start: DOM listeners for the idle timer (wheel, mouse moves) and the \"seen a key or pad\" flags */\n45:    this.wall = typeof performance !== 'undefined';   // in a page the idle timer is real time (a slow frame doesn't stretch it)\n47:    const bump = () => { this.idle = 0; if (this.wall) this.lastAt = performance.now(); };\n59:  /** each step: the idle timer (any action, stick or pad button resets it) */\n62:    if (this.wall) this.idle = (performance.now() - this.lastAt) / 1000; else this.idle += dt;\n64:    if (I.anyPressed() || Math.hypot(pm[0], pm[1]) > .3 || (pa && Math.hypot(pa[0], pa[1]) > .3)) { this.idle = 0; if (this.wall) this.lastAt = performance.now(); if (I.lastDevice === 'gamepad') this.sawPad = true; }\n67:  reset() { this.idle = 0; if (this.wall) this.lastAt = performance.now(); },\n42:Attract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game. \n53:Touch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afaa845e-3b4d-4028-b42c-2fc9910c5b5f","uuid":"c283d0bc-db62-4730-b53b-394eea6bfcd9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:56:07.946Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"      if (game.input.touchEnabled !== undefined) game.input.touchEnabled = false;\n    },\n    update(dt) {\n      S7.Input.tick(dt); titleT += dt;\n      sim.update(dt, S7.noIntents()); pres.step(dt); snd();\n      const m = S7.ui.modal;\n      if (m) {\n        S7.ui.update();\n        if (!S7.ui.modal && S7.ui.kind === null && m instanceof DifficultyModal && m.result && m.result !== 'back') { S7.newGame(m.result); return; }\n        \n      } else {\n        const touch = S7.touchOnly();\n        if (touch) { const c = game.input.clicked && game.input.clicked(); if (c && UI.hit(c, ...(this.setBox || [0, 0, 0, 0]))) game.menu('settings'); }\n        e